            "review_title": "Review at Giay Bac (Tin Foil Grill)",
            "review_text": "Deepak DB\nMumbai, India938 contributions\n0\nPurely Local Fare\nJun 2019 • Family\nAs a tourist we wanted to dine like a local with locals and not a touristy place. We found this place with good ratings on local site and decided to try it out. It so happened that the maps couldn't take us there easily and eventually we landed in an alley off the main road. One of the local boys hanging out understood our plight but of course he could speak No English. When we pointed out to the name of restaurant he said it was the same place where we were standing. \n\nThe name was put up discreetly with low lighting and the place was packed with locals who started looking at us some curiously and few smiling. The staff too had a similar expressing may be out of worry how will we manage these guests.\n\nOne of the hostesses who could speak basic english helped us,which we needed, as we had limitiation on type of meats which we could eat.\n\nThe locals devor the family pot which has a broth steaming on table and you have variety of meats, veggies to dip and enjoy. The next best on the menu was the Tin Foil Grilled meats with choice of sauces. Most of the food is spicy and even the ones which we opted for was fairly spicy.\n\nThe food was good, totally dined like a local. The service was good and quick. The decor is basis but the pricing is bit high since it is located in District 1 which is the premium locale. They don't accept credit card so do keep that in mind.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten June 26, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
