            "review_text": "CrabisGOOD\nTaguig City, Philippines378 contributions\n0\nBest Meal of Our Short 2 day trip to hcm\nNov 2016 • Family\nThis small restaurant is nestled in an alley, but it was full when we were there. We received excellent service by the owner and we're very pleased with the experience. The menu is affordable and unique.\n\nWe tried the chicken curry, fried soft crab, strawberry pudding, almond tofu dessert, cha gio (not what we expected as it was very mayo based, but good), meats 1,2,3 on the top page, sour cabbage, dried mangos, and salty fish fried rice. Every thing was very good. Of the meats, I enjoyed the meat roll/meat balls. It was fun rolling the rice wrappers with our son and it was delicious.\n\nEverything was well cooked and it was a great meal. Our best overall meal in hcm.\nRead more\nWritten November 2, 2016",
