            "review_text": "Paul M\nBuffalo, New York403 contributions\n0\nFresh Summer Rolls Made Right\nJul 2016 • Friends\nThere are good restaurants where you can wrap your own Vietnamese spring rolls (or fresh summer rolls). But the rice paper in some of these is tough and chewy, from a store-bought package. Try Giấy Bạc, which is a short walk from Bến Thành Market (Chợ Bến Thành). \n\nAt Giấy Bạc you select the meat and vegetables you want in your fresh rolls, and these are brought on small plates. Then, you receive a tray full of small dishes that at first appear empty. On these dishes are the rice papers in which you will create your fresh summer rolls. The rice paper is soft and fresh ... almost invisible. Create your roll, dip it in the fish sauce (nước mắm) and enjoy.\nAt the end of the meal, your server will count the number of empty rice paper plates to determine your bill (plus the meat and vegetables you ordered, of course).\nI went with a friend for dinner and it was a nice evening. We also had the soft shell crab, which was superb.\nIf you are in the Backpacker District, or near Bến Thành Market, this would be a good choice for lunch or dinner. It is on a side street, so be sure you have a good map, or ask for directions as you near the street it is on.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 29, 2016",
